  "title": "The Message I Deleted",
  "brief": "Female lead. She has ignored messages from her sister, then feels hurt when the invitations stop. She drafts an accusation in her bedroom. Her sister replies that she thought she wanted space. At her desk she writes the excuses she was about to use, then a truthful apology. She walks outside, returns to the phone and admits she wanted her sister to keep asking but never said so. The reply is kind but honest about being hurt. She apologizes without asking to be instantly forgiven. End at her desk writing what she wants to say when they talk tomorrow. One visible human. Rain outside, a ticking wall clock, concrete messages, anger giving way to remorse and cautious relief.",
